@1000 = ~Hello.~
@1001 = ~A talking rabbit? I thought I had seen everything.~
@1002 = ~Greetings to you, little rabbit.~
@1003 = ~I am not a rabbit, I am a doe rabbit. And I can speak because I am Agenor's familiar.~
@1004 = ~Familiar? That's impossible, Agenor cannot be a mage.~
@1005 = ~And why, pray tell, could he not be?~
@1006 = ~It is common knowledge that dwarves cannot be wizards....~
@1007 = ~How narrow-minded of you... We live in a world of magic, where anything is possible. Agenor is a mage, I am his familiar, it is strange and exceptional, but certainly not impossible. Bah, I grow tired of speaking with such close-minded people. Go talk to my master about this, I am sure he will be delighted to tell you his story.~
@1008 = ~A familiar? So Agenor really is a mage?~
@1009 = ~No kidding. Did you think he wore robes simply because of the way they looked on him?~
@10011 = ~No, of course not.~
@10012 = ~Then here are the facts. Agenor is a wizard, I am his familiar, and I am wasting my time speaking with a dullard who has nothing to offer me. Go speak to Agenor instead; it will be far more useful.~
@10013 = ~Greetings to you, little doe rabbit.~
@10014 = ~That is better. Hello.~
@10015 = ~I am not a rabbit, I am a doe rabbit. I am Agenor's familiar.~
@10016 = ~And what is your name?~
@10017 = ~Basic wisdom dictates that one should not reveal one's name to just anyone.~
@10018 = ~Very well. And so?....~
@10019 = ~And so nothing. Go speak to Agenor instead of wasting my time with foolish questions.~